<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Godefroy Maurice de La Tour d'Auvergne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1636–1721</span> · Also known as Godefroy Maurice de La Tour d'Auvergne, Duke of Bouillon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Godefroy Maurice de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-la-tour-dauvergne">La Tour d'Auvergne</a> was a French nobleman, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederic-maurice-de-la-tour-dauvergne">Duke of Bouillon</a> and a nephew of Marshal Turenne. After French troops took Bouillon in 1678, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> gave him the duchy, which his family had long claimed, to hold under French protection, and his descendants ruled it until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. He also served as Grand Chamberlain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/godefroy-maurice-de-la-tour-dauvergne.jpg" alt="Godefroy Maurice de La Tour d'Auvergne" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Nanteuil · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GodefroyMauricedeLaTour_dAuvergneNanteuil.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
